hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16098","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Maruf, meaning Ibn Wasil, narrated to us, he said, Hafsah bint Talq, a woman of the tribe, narrated to me in the year ninety, from Abu Umayrah, he said, we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, and a man came with a tray upon it dates, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is this, charity or gift. He said, charity. He said, so bring it forward to the people, and Hasan, prayers of Allah and His peace upon him, was crawling before him, and the boy took a date and put it in his mouth, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put his finger in the mouth of the boy and removed the date and threw it, then he said: We, the family of Muhammad, charity is not lawful for us. So I said to Maruf, is Abu Umayr your grandfather. He said, the grandfather of my father. He said."
"16099","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said, Maruf narrated to us, from Hafsah bint Talq, from Abu Umayrah Usayd ibn Malik, grandfather of Maruf, he said, we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the like of it."
